  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A spherical shell of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> mass and radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is rolling with angular speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi></math> on horizontal plane (as shown in figure). The magnitude of angular momentum of the shell about the origin <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#969;</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;will be</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/0eac515c-ef27-40a6-9811-97f3b6cae570-image.png\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 124px;\" />&nbsp;</p>",
    "image": null
